|Dec|Int|Lng|Obj|SByte|Short|Sng|Str|Type|UInt|ULng|UShort)|Char|Class|Const|Continue|Date|Decimal|Declare|Default|Delegate|Dim|DirectCast|Do|Double|Each|Else(?:If)?|End(?:If)?|Enum|Erase|Error|Event|Exit|Finally|For|Friend|Function|Get(?:Type|XMLNamespace)?|Global|GoSub|GoTo|Handles|If|Implements|Imports|In|Inherits|Integer|Interface|Is|IsNot|Let|Lib|Like|Long|Loop|Me|Mod|Module|Must(?:Inherit|Override)|My(?:Base|Class)|Namespace|Narrowing|New|Next|Not(?:Inheritable|Overridable)?|Object|Of|On|Operator|Option(?:al)?|Or(?:Else)?|Out|Overloads|Overridable|Overrides|ParamArray|Partial|Private|Property|Protected|Public|RaiseEvent|ReadOnly|ReDim|RemoveHandler|Resume|Return|SByte|Select|Set|Shadows|Shared|short|Single|Static|Step|Stop|String|Structure|Sub|SyncLock|Then|Throw|To|Try|TryCast|TypeOf|U(?:Integer|Long|Short)|Using|Variant|Wend|When|While|Widening|With(?:Events)?|WriteOnly|Xor)\\b/i,\n+\t'operator': [\n+\t\t/[+\\-*/\\\\^<=>&#@$%!]/,\n+\t\t{\n+\t\t\tpattern: /([^\\S\\r\\n])_(?=[^\\S\\r\\n]*[\\r\\n])/,\n+\t\t\tlookbehind: true\n+\t\t}\n+\t],\n+\t'punctuation': /[{}().,:?]/\n+};\n+\n+Prism.languages.vb = Prism.languages['visual-basic'];\n\\ No newline at end of file\ndiff --git a/server.log b/server.log\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 00000000..7e1f1905\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/server.log\n@@ -0,0 +1,9 @@\n+Serving HTTP on 0.0.0.0 port 8000 (http://0.0.0.0:8000/) ...\n+127.0.0.1 - - [04/Jun/2026 03:19:02] \"GET /test_vb_line_continuation.html HTTP/1.1\" 200 -\n+127.0.0.1 - - [04/Jun/2026 03:19:02] \"GET /themes/prism.css HTTP/1.1\" 200 -\n+127.0.0.1 - - [04/Jun/2026 03:19:02] \"GET /components/prism-core.js HTTP/1.1\" 200 -\n+127.0.0.1 - - [04/Jun/2026 03:19:02] \"GET /components/prism-visual-basic.js HTTP/1.1\" 200 -\n+127.0.0.1 - - [04/Jun/2026 03:21:05] \"GET /test_vb_line_continuation.html HTTP/1.1\" 304 -\n+127.0.0.1 - - [04/Jun/2026 03:21:05] \"GET /components/prism-core.js HTTP/1.1\" 304 -\n+127.0.0.1 - - [04/Jun/2026 03:21:05] \"GET /themes/prism.css HTTP/1.1\" 304 -\n+127.0.0.1 - - [04/Jun/2026 03:21:05] \"GET /components/prism-visual-basic.js HTTP/1.1\" 200 -\ndiff --git a/temp.js b/temp.js\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 00000000..e69de29b\ndiff --git a/test_comprehensive_comments.js b/test_comprehensive_comments.js\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 00000000..c8268e9b\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/test_comprehensive_comments.js\n@@ -0,0 +1,108 @@\n+// Comprehensive test for Visual Basic comments including line continuation\n+const Prism = require('./components/prism-core.js');\n+require('./components/prism-visual-basic.js');\n+\n+console.log(\"=== COMPREHENSIVE VISUAL BASIC COMMENT TEST ===\\n\");\n+\n+// Test cases combining existing functionality and new line continuation\n+const testCases = [\n+    {\n+        name: \"Existing single-line comments\",\n+        code: \"'\\n' Foo \\\"bar\\\"\\n'\\n' Foobar\",\n+        shouldWork: true\n+    },\n+    {\n+        name: \"Existing REM comments\", \n+        code: \"REM\\nREM Foobar\",\n+        shouldWork: true\n+    },\n+    {\n+        name: \"NEW: Comment with line continuation\",\n+        code: \"' This comment continues _\\nonto the next line\\nDim x As Integer\",\n+        shouldWork: true,\n+        expectSingleCommentToken: true\n+    },\n+    {\n+        name: \"NEW: REM comment with line continuation\",\n+        code: \"REM This REM comment continues _\\nonto the next line\\nDim y As String\", \n+        shouldWork: true,\n+        expectSingleCommentToken: true\n+    },\n+    {\n+        name: \"NEW: Multiple line continuations\",\n+        code: \"' Comment spans _\\nmultiple _\\nlines here\\nDim z As Boolean\",\n+        shouldWork: true,\n+        expectSingleCommentToken: true\n+    },\n+    {\n+        name: \"Mixed: Normal and continued comments\",\n+        code: \"' Normal comment\\n' Continued comment _\\nwith continuation\\n' Another normal\",\n+        shouldWork: true\n+    }\n+];\n+\n+let allTestsPassed = true;\n+\n+testCases.forEach((testCase, index) => {\n+    console.log(`\\n--- Test ${index + 1}: ${testCase.name} ---`);\n+    console.log(`Code: ${JSON.stringify(testCase.code)}`);\n+    \n+    try {\n+        const tokens = Prism.tokenize(testCase.code, Prism.languages['visual-basic']);\n+        \n+        // Count comment tokens\n+        const commentTokens = tokens.filter(token => \n+            typeof token === 'object' && token.type === 'comment'\n+        );\n+        \n+        console.log(`Found ${commentTokens.length} comment token(s):`);\n+        commentTokens.forEach((token, i) => {\n+            const content = typeof token.content === 'string' ? token.content : \n+                           Array.isArray(token.content) ? token.content.map(t => \n+                               typeof t === 'string' ? t : t.content || '[object]'\n+                           ).join('') : String(token.content);\n+            console.log(`  ${i + 1}: \"${content}\"`);\n+        });\n+        \n+        // Special check for line continuation tests\n+        if (testCase.expectSingleCommentToken) {\n+            const firstCommentToken = commentTokens[0];\n+            if (firstCommentToken) {\n+                const content = typeof firstCommentToken.content === 'string' ? \n+                               firstCommentToken.content : \n+                               Array.isArray(firstCommentToken.content) ? \n+                               firstCommentToken.content.map(t => typeof t === 'string' ? t : t.content || '').join('') :\n+                               String(firstCommentToken.content);\n+                \n+                const hasMultipleLines = content.includes('\\n');\n+                console.log(`  \u2713 Single comment token spans multiple lines: ${hasMultipleLines}`);\n+                \n+                if (!hasMultipleLines) {\n+                    console.log(`  \u2717 Expected multi-line comment but got: \"${content}\"`);\n+                    allTestsPassed = false;\n+                }\n+            } else {\n+                console.log(`  \u2717 No comment token found`);\n+                allTestsPassed = false;\n+            }\n+        }\n+        \n+        console.log(`  \u2713 Test passed`);\n+        \n+    } catch (error) {\n+        console.log(`  \u2717 Test failed with error: ${error.message}`);\n+        allTestsPassed = false;\n+    }\n+});\n+\n+console.log(`\\n=== FINAL RESULT ===`);\n+if (allTestsPassed) {\n+    console.log(\"\ud83c\udf89 ALL TESTS PASSED! The Visual Basic comment line continuation fix is working correctly.\");\n+    console.log(\"\u2705 Existing functionality preserved\");\n+    console.log(\"\u2705 New line continuation feature working\");\n+    console.log(\"\u2705 No regressions detected\");\n+} else {\n+    console.log(\"\u274c Some tests failed. Please review the implementation.\");\n+}\n+\n+console.log(\"\\nTest completed!\");\n\\ No newline at end of file\ndiff --git a/test_existing_comments.js b/test_existing_comments.js\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 00000000..c3faf0c8\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/test_existing_comments.js\n@@ -0,0 +1,65 @@\n+// Test script to verify existing Visual Basic comment tests still work\n+const Prism = require('./components/prism-core.js');\n+require('./components/prism-visual-basic.js');\n+\n+// Test case from existing comment_feature.test\n+const testCode = `'\n+' Foo \"bar\"\n+'\n+' Foobar\n+'\n+' Foobar\n+REM\n+REM Foobar`;\n+\n+console.log(\"Testing existing Visual Basic comment functionality...\\n\");\n+console.log(\"Test code:\");\n+console.log(JSON.stringify(testCode));\n+console.log(\"\\n\");\n+\n+const tokens = Prism.tokenize(testCode, Prism.languages['visual-basic']);\n+\n+console.log(\"Actual tokens found:\");\n+tokens.forEach((token, i) => {\n+    if (typeof token === 'string') {\n+        console.log(`  ${i}: \"${token}\" (string)`);\n+    } else {\n+        console.log(`  ${i}: \"${token.content}\" (${token.type})`);\n+        if (token.content && typeof token.content === 'object') {\n+            console.log(`    Content details:`, token.content);\n+        }\n+    }\n+});\n+\n+// Expected tokens from the test file\n+const expectedComments = [\n+    \"'\",\n+    \"' Foo \\\"bar\\\"\", \n+    \"'\",\n+    \"' Foobar\",\n+    \"'\", \n+    \"' Foobar\",\n+    \"REM\",\n+    \"REM Foobar\"\n+];\n+\n+console.log(\"\\nExpected comment tokens:\");\n+expectedComments.forEach((comment, i) => {\n+    console.log(`  ${i}: \"${comment}\"`);\n+});\n+\n+// Verify that all comment tokens are found\n+let commentTokens = tokens.filter(token => \n+    typeof token === 'object' && token.type === 'comment'\n+);\n+\n+console.log(`\\nFound ${commentTokens.length} comment tokens (expected ${expectedComments.length})`);\n+\n+commentTokens.forEach((token, i) => {\n+    const content = typeof token.content === 'string' ? token.content : \n+                   Array.isArray(token.content) ? token.content.join('') : \n+                   String(token.content);\n+    console.log(`Comment ${i + 1}: \"${content}\"`);\n+});\n+\n+console.log(\"\\nTest completed!\");\n\\ No newline at end of file\ndiff --git a/test_fix_verification.js b/test_fix_verification.js\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 00000000..9c9c6a5a\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/test_fix_verification.js\n@@ -0,0 +1,67 @@\n+// Test script to verify the Visual Basic line continuation fix\n+const fs = require('fs');\n+const path = require('path');\n+\n+// Load Prism\n+const Prism = require('./components/prism-core.js');\n+require('./components/prism-visual-basic.js');\n+\n+// Test cases\n+const testCases = [\n+    {\n+        name: \"Single line comment with continuation\",\n+        code: \"' This is a comment that continues _\\non the next line\\nDim x As Integer\",\n+        expectedTokens: [\"comment\", \"keyword\", \"keyword\", \"keyword\"]\n+    },\n+    {\n+        name: \"REM comment with continuation\", \n+        code: \"REM This is a REM comment that continues _\\non the next line\\nDim y As String\",\n+        expectedTokens: [\"comment\", \"keyword\", \"keyword\", \"keyword\"]\n+    },\n+    {\n+        name: \"Multiple line continuations\",\n+        code: \"' This comment spans _\\nmultiple _\\nlines with continuations\\nDim z As Boolean\",\n+        expectedTokens: [\"comment\", \"keyword\", \"keyword\", \"keyword\"]\n+    },\n+    {\n+        name: \"Normal single-line comment\",\n+        code: \"' This is a normal comment\\nDim normal As Integer\",\n+        expectedTokens: [\"comment\", \"keyword\", \"keyword\", \"keyword\"]\n+    }\n+];\n+\n+console.log(\"Testing Visual Basic line continuation fix...\\n\");\n+\n+testCases.forEach((testCase, index) => {\n+    console.log(`Test ${index + 1}: ${testCase.name}`);\n+    console.log(`Code: ${JSON.stringify(testCase.code)}`);\n+    \n+    const tokens = Prism.tokenize(testCase.code, Prism.languages['visual-basic']);\n+    \n+    console.log(\"Tokens found:\");\n+    tokens.forEach((token, i) => {\n+        if (typeof token === 'string') {\n+            console.log(`  ${i}: \"${token}\" (string)`);\n+        } else {\n+            console.log(`  ${i}: \"${token.content}\" (${token.type})`);\n+        }\n+    });\n+    \n+    // Check if the first token is a comment and contains line continuation\n+    const firstToken = tokens[0];\n+    if (typeof firstToken === 'object' && firstToken.type === 'comment') {\n+        const hasLineContinuation = firstToken.content.includes('_\\n');\n+        console.log(`\u2713 Comment token contains line continuation: ${hasLineContinuation}`);\n+        \n+        if (hasLineContinuation) {\n+            const lines = firstToken.content.split('\\n');\n+            console.log(`\u2713 Comment spans ${lines.length} lines`);\n+        }\n+    } else {\n+        console.log(\"\u2717 First token is not a comment\");\n+    }\n+    \n+    console.log(\"---\\n\");\n+});\n+\n+console.log(\"Test completed!\");\n\\ No newline at end of file\ndiff --git a/test_line_continuation_comments.test b/test_line_continuation_comments.test\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 00000000..af00b1c4\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/test_line_continuation_comments.test\n@@ -0,0 +1,19 @@\n+' Comment with line continuation _\n+should be highlighted as one token\n+REM Comment with line continuation _\n+should also be highlighted as one token\n+' Multiple line _\n+continuation _\n+comment\n+\n+----------------------------------------------------\n+\n+[\n+\t[\"comment\", [\"' Comment with line continuation _\\nshould be highlighted as one token\"]],\n+\t[\"comment\", [[\"keyword\", \"REM\"], \" Comment with line continuation _\\nshould also be highlighted as one token\"]],\n+\t[\"comment\", [\"' Multiple line _\\ncontinuation _\\ncomment\"]]\n+]\n+\n+----------------------------------------------------\n+\n+Checks for comments with line continuation.\n\\ No newline at end of file\ndiff --git a/test_vb_line_continuation.html b/test_vb_line_continuation.html\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 00000000..a2e71cc9\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/test_vb_line_continuation.html\n@@ -0,0 +1,60 @@\n+<!DOCTYPE html>\n+<html>\n+<head>\n+    <title>Visual Basic Line Continuation Test</title>\n+    <link href=\"themes/prism.css\" rel=\"stylesheet\" />\n+    <style>\n+        body { font-family: Arial, sans-serif; margin: 20px; }\n+        .test-case { margin: 20px 0; border: 1px solid #ccc; padding: 10px; }\n+        .test-title { font-weight: bold; margin-bottom: 10px; }\n+        pre { background: #f5f5f5; padding: 10px; }\n+    </style>\n+</head>\n+<body>\n+    <h1>Visual Basic Line Continuation Comment Test</h1>\n+    \n+    <div class=\"test-case\">\n+        <div class=\"test-title\">Test 1: Comment with line continuation (ISSUE)</div>\n+        <pre><code class=\"language-visual-basic\">' This is a comment that continues _\n+on the next line\n+Dim x As Integer</code></pre>\n+    </div>\n+    \n+    <div class=\"test-case\">\n+        <div class=\"test-title\">Test 2: REM comment with line continuation</div>\n+        <pre><code class=\"language-visual-basic\">REM This is a REM comment that continues _\n+on the next line\n+Dim y As String</code></pre>\n+    </div>\n+    \n+    <div class=\"test-case\">\n+        <div class=\"test-title\">Test 3: Multiple line continuations</div>\n+        <pre><code class=\"language-visual-basic\">' This comment spans _\n+multiple _\n+lines with continuations\n+Dim z As Boolean</code></pre>\n+    </div>\n+    \n+    <div class=\"test-case\">\n+        <div class=\"test-title\">Test 4: InputBox example from issue</div>\n+        <pre><code class=\"language-visual-basic\">' strDate = Application.InputBox(Prompt:=\"Please Enter Beginning Date to Locate:\", _\n+Title:=\"DATE FIND\", Default:=Format(Date, \"Short Date\"), Type:=2)\n+Dim result As String</code></pre>\n+    </div>\n+    \n+    <div class=\"test-case\">\n+        <div class=\"test-title\">Test 5: Normal single-line comment (should work)</div>\n+        <pre><code class=\"language-visual-basic\">' This is a normal comment\n+Dim normal As Integer</code></pre>\n+    </div>\n+    \n+    <div class=\"test-case\">\n+        <div class=\"test-title\">Test 6: Code with line continuation (not comment)</div>\n+        <pre><code class=\"language-visual-basic\">Dim longString As String = \"This is a long string \" & _\n+                                  \"that continues on next line\"</code></pre>\n+    </div>\n+\n+    <script src=\"components/prism-core.js\"></script>\n+    <script src=\"components/prism-visual-basic.js\"></script>\n+</body>\n+</html>\n\\ No newline at end of file", "model_name_or_path": "llm.claude4"}